se, and the true picture is four different wrong outcomes rather than one. ***
tools\pipeline\matrix.html:562:* *** THE FINDING IS A FLAW IN THE LADDER IT WROTE THIS MORNING: THE RUNG ORDER AND THE PRIORITY ORDER DIVERGE. *** b120r&#x27;s witness is rung 4 (an instrumented boot) while armbdt&#x27;s is rung 3 (a probe), so the ladder&#x27;s clause &#x27;order items by the strongest witness that exists TODAY&#x27; puts b120r FIRST. That is wrong for scheduling: b120r&#x27;s measured guest-visible symptom is NIL (told-98 and told-35 give byte-identical transcripts) while armbdt CORRUPTS GUEST DATA. RUNG MEASURES REACHABILITY-PROOF STRENGTH, NOT HARM. The carrier clause is corrected.
