tools\pipeline\matrix.html:1145:THE WITNESS THAT WOULD SETTLE IT, rung 3 on -E cats: program counter 0 to ~18 Hz, free-run 200 ms, read the 8259 IRR (expect bit0), write specific-EOI 0x60 to 0x7c000020, free-run ~5 ms, read IRR again. Draining correctly =&gt; 0 (next tick due at ~55 ms); no drain =&gt; 1 again on the very next device tick. Clean discriminator, no source change. — evidence: build/gxemul -E cats device order; grep census of the drain sites</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-held"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-held"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">witnessunwired</span><span class="ttl">witnessunwired  Section K passes a row whose witness artefact no gate ever executes</span><span class="tip">witnessunwired  Section K passes a row whose witness artefact no gate ever executes — HOLD: Found by a ninth-seat review. The floodclass detector round would force the wiring as a side effect, so it may not need its own round. — witness: harness:check_witness.py&#x27;s own header, which states the limitation the row describes -- so the premise is verifiable by reading the tool. — note: *** EVIDENCE 202