-fatalised the WIDTH guard only; the width test is evaluated FIRST, so a legal `ld` still reaches the kill.  *** THE ORDERING OBLIGATION IS ALREADY RECORDED IN #497&#x27;s ROUND BLOCK AND IS THE REASON THIS ROW MUST NOT BE CLOSED BY THE CHECKER: fixing sgirekills will turn a GREEN GATE RED BY SUCCEEDING, six rows&#x27; worth. ***  It therefore inherits the oracle-correction ordering -- re-pin the six rows FIRST, measure the committed build RED under the new expectations, THEN edit the code.  A row whose own detector must invert is exactly the case the shipped-work heuristic cannot read.
