tools\pipeline\matrix.html:5687:*** ORDERING: THE SEVERITY ORDER INVERTS.  This LOW row runs FIRST, as a prerequisite of the HIGH one. ***  LOW is the label; first is the schedule; the two are severed deliberately, because ranked LOW and left in severity order it would sit behind the round that depends on it.  Cost is about zero calendar time -- sgirekills still owes its own rung-3 witness and that work parallelises with this small shift round. — evidence: dev_sgi_re.c re_tex[112] then re_linear_a[32]; debugger_cmds.c put d = printf not guard; sgi_re_width_probe.py stores at base+8 greps re_tex[1]; sgi_re_unmapped_probe.py 0x6d8 greps re_tex[27]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — ANSWERED 2026-08-31.  (The marker it was held under is DEFANGED: HELD-AWAITING-SEAT codex, cleared -- a verbatim copy re-arms three tools, and a wrongly-live marker in a regress phase is additionally counted as a seat ANSWER that never happened.)
