an class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">holdphase</span><span class="ttl">the hold-marker discriminator was implemented with `&gt;=` where the carrier says LATER, and six holds were cleared by SAME-DATE siblings written by the batch that created the marker</span><span class="tip">the hold-marker discriminator was implemented with `&gt;=` where the carrier says LATER, and six holds were cleared by SAME-DATE siblings written by the batch that created the marker — witness: harness:MEASURED by the codex and opus5 seats on the #497b pass-2 panel, independently, and confirmed here row by row before reverting.  SIX markers were wrongly cleared, ALL of them phase=regress / seat=fable5: ns16550, carrier, es438, sh4sci, wdcdataoutdrain, and wdccdbmidxfer entry [26].  *** THIS FIELD PREVIOUSLY NAMED THE SIXTH AS &#x27;research/opus5, answered at review&#x27;.  THAT IS THE MARKER THE COMMIT **KEPT** -- disposition (b) -- NOT the one it cleared.  Caught by the fable5 seat; I had copied the framing from another seat&#x27;s table without checking which entry it pointed at. ***  widthkillclass was the one CORRECT clearance: held at review, all seven named seats answered at review.  A strictly-later + same-stage test keeps all six and clears that one.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">gxprobepccache</span><span class="ttl">gxprobe cached the pc across `step`, so a driver that stepped without _exec_at() had its next pc assignment silently skipped -- a detector row that could not fail</span><span class="tip">gxprobe cached the pc across `step`, so a driver that stepped without _exec_at() had its next pc assignment silently skipped -- a detector row that could not fail — witness: harness:MEASURED by the #497-family measuring seat and re-verified here.  `gxprobe.py` skips a redundant register assignment when `cache_regs` is on; `_exec_at()` pops the cached pc after stepping, but a driver calling `send(&quot;step&quot;)` DIRECTLY did not -- so its next `set_reg(&quot;pc&quot;, a)` was dropped as redundant.  The transcript is unambiguous: the first access carries a `pc=` line, the second and third do not, and they execute `nop`.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">pcc2widthkills</span><span class="ttl">dev_pcc2.c: TEN live width kills (of twelve guards -- #119 already fixed two in this same file, and its shape is the answer)</span><span class="tip">dev_pcc2.c: TEN live width kills (of twelve guards -- #119 already fixed two in this same file, and its shape is the answer) — commits: b78bb0f — witness: probe:regress/pcc2_width_witness.py -- rung 3, 4/10 on the committed build (three aligned accesses each exit1, four controls green); artifacts/pcc2widthkills/witness_20260903_PREFIX.out — note: *** PASS 2 FOUND SIX CLEAN SWEEPS of the shipped 60-row detector (b78bb0f), the smallest ONE CHARACTER; the REPAIR is on disk, uncommitted: 82 rows (+8 IPL/MASK, +7 per-arm channels, +2 latch cardinality, +1 operand-swap, +4 odd-arm fall-through). Measured: part 1 nine mutants all killed at 78 (part1/driver.log); the builder&#x27;s pass 3 killed all six sweeps at 78 and its 3b showed four fall-through TOTAL SWEEPS at 78 that its 3c kills 81/82 each at 82 (opus_pass3_20260903/); part 2 (M_IDATA_GENCTL vs 82) pending at the time of this note. PRETABLE.out written before table 2 (Section 0 records that table 1 had none). OWED before commit: part 2&#x27;s sentinel, propagate dev_pcc2.c to build/ build-asan/ gxsec-build + two-part clearance, gate 14, CHANGELOG block from the logs, then PASS 3 (the eight other seats; the builder&#x27;s pass 3 is one seat of it).  *** Superseded text, kept: FIXED (uncommitted at the time of writing; commit follows). Twelve width-guard blocks -&gt; direction split: reads ACCEPT (the memcpy above the switch already served them; the tree&#x27;s own header says wide access is LEGAL), writes DECLINE + per-instance 12-bit latch. DELETE is measurably wrong (big-endian compose: the low byte is the neighbour&#x27;s lane) -- M_DELETE killed. The seven odd arms are OPERATOR-reachable (debugger put h, MEASURED) -- all twelve converted, M_OPKILL killed through that path. Detector 60 rows, gate 14 626/0, PREFIX 14/60, BASE 60/60, seven mutants zero sweeps. Design pass on 6 of 9 + one measurement (Opus x2 529, grok x2 CLI). Filed: pcc2c040kill (HIGH), pcc2counter8 (MED), pcc2widecompose. Owes pass 2.  2026-09-04 FIX REVIEW (owner directive): GPT-6 Astra (max) APPROVES the fix, DOES NOT CLOSE; Fable 5.1 GO-WITH-CHANGES.  Seven Astra findings confirmed from the tree; the main loop graded two as open floor cells -- the five HUH?-clear arms were then MEASURED HELD by announce-count rows (part 13 M_HUHV 249/251; the rbq rows strengthen the channel, L4 + coverage, not L2), the INT-set/count-0 cell awaits M_ZINT -&gt; PASS 13 owed: 9 rows (242 -&gt; 251), 7 mutants, gate, panel.  Astra dissents on the floor bound (Opus strength-t); the adjudicator adopts Fable&#x27;s floor + the generating set.  PASS 13 PANEL COMPLETE 9/9 (2026-09-05 02:17-03:46).  RULING: PASS 14 OWED -- the class closure (three file-reading seats derived the same two gaps: the generating set one-sided at the two new INT cells; the INT axis not crossed with the other count), graded L1 (uncommitted detector material).  The pass-13 state is COMMITTED with the obligation OPEN (thirteen uncommitted passes were the larger exposure); pass 14 is drafted (fix_pcc2_p15.py: +18 rows -&gt; 269, 8 mutants, PRETABLE_pass14, plus a pre-repair breach witness part14pre) and runs after the pcc2defaultkill fix ships (owner priority: critical first).
tools\pipeline\matrix.html:5862:duplicate that passed the gate and had to be withdrawn; the check is cheap and it worked here.)*</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-02 — CONFIRMED — OWED BY THE ROUND, from the same adjudication: (a) the CONTRACT must state the 5-reachable/7-unreachable split rather than claim ten; (b) a rung-3 witness is BUILDABLE and should be attempted before recording documented-only -- planted m88k halfword load at 0xfff42002 on mvme187, pre-fix symptom is process exit, with VECBASE&#x27;s nonzero reset (0x0f) as the device-signature control; (c) FLAGGED NOT ASSERTED by the seat, and the round owes an answer: whether any real mvme187 driver performs the wide WRITES the decline will refuse.  Its own words: &#x27;that is a reading, not a measurement&#x27;. — evidence: _scratchpad/fable_adj_20260902 (Agent seat, model self-declared claude-fable-5)</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-01 — MANUAL — REVISE -- the uniform design misdescribes reads, and one shared latch is wrong.  *The proposed uniform &#x27;decline + latched announce&#x27; design MISDESCRIBES READS, and a single shared latch would suppress distinct diagnostics.*  Both halves are now confirmed: the read path really does compute its value before the kill (see grok), so describing all twelve arms as one uniform decline is wrong; and a single latch across ten arms means the first wide access anywhere silences the diagnostic for the other nine, which is the shared-latch failure `#498` measured at 23/25 and this session measured again as `M_BITALIAS&#x27;. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260901_183841_pcc2p1</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-01 — UNKNOWN — [NOT-FIRED]  *** RESERVED FOR MEASUREMENT by owner ruling.  NOT a seat failure and NOT agreement. *** — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260901_183841_pcc2p1</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-01 — MANUAL — FOUND THE THING THAT RESCOPES THE ROW.  *** IT ASKED WHETHER THE TOP-OF-FUNCTION `memcpy&#x27; ALREADY MAKES WIDE READS SUCCEED, AND THAT QUESTION CORRECTS MY BRIEF. ***  dev_pcc2.c has, BEFORE the switch: `if (writeflag == MEM_READ) { if (relative_addr + len &lt;= PCC2_SIZE) memcpy(data, d-&gt;pcctwo_reg + relative_addr, len); ... }&#x27;.  MAIN LOOP TRACED THE CONTROL FLOW: the memcpy fills `data&#x27; and then FALLS THROUGH to the switch, so a wide READ is SERVED CORRECTLY AND THEN THE HOST DIES OVER IT at `len != 1&#x27;.
tools\pipeline\matrix.html:5866:**CORRECT, AND NOW EVIDENCED.**  memory_rw.c calls `mem-&gt;devices[i].f(cpu, mem, paddr, data, len, writeflag, extra)&#x27; ONCE, with `len&#x27; passed through.  There is no loop around it.  `len&#x27; is written in exactly two places: a PAGE-STRADDLING split path, and a clamp to the device&#x27;s own end which prints a diagnostic.  An aligned halfword at 0x0002 neither straddles a page nor reaches the device end, so it arrives as ONE call with len == 2.  The leg holds -- but glm was right that I had asserted it, and this is the second time today a seat caught me presenting an untraced leg as settled. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260901_183841_pcc2p1</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-01 — MANUAL — not ratifiable as written; convert the #119 sites; names the escaping mutant.  Q1 decline + latched announce with a PER-INSTANCE bit.  Q2 addition licence NOT satisfied without one further fact.  Q3 **CONVERT** the two `#119&#x27; sites rather than leaving the file with two latch idioms.  Q4 the smallest escaping mutant is `|=&#x27; -&gt; `=&#x27; in a per-arm bitmask -- which is the same family as the flood mutant a sibling round measured today (`|=&#x27; dropped), and confirms that the latch&#x27;s ASSIGNMENT operator is the fragile part, not its test. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260901_183841_pcc2p1</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-01 — MANUAL — same leg, independently; and the licence warrant is insufficient.  Reached the device-dispatch gap independently of glm.  Also: the Q2 warrant is insufficient under the addition licence **because dev_pcc2 is SINGLE-INSTANCE** -- so the per-instance-latch argument (one instance silencing another) has no instance to bite on here, and the transferred warrant does not transfer cleanly.  That is the sharpest form of the objection and it is not answered by pointing at the house idiom. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260901_183841_pcc2p1</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-03 — CONFIRMED — Self-declared claude-fable-5-1 (a claim). *** THE TREE ALREADY KNEW WIDE ACCESS IS LEGAL: mvme_pcctworeg.h:9-10 says PCC2 registers can be accessed as 8/16/32 bits -- neither the brief nor the 2026-09-02 adjudication cited it. Refutes FAULT; reframes DECLINE as refusing a hardware-legal access. *** DELETE is measurably WRONG for writes: memory_readmax64 composes big-endian so (uint8_t)idata is the HIGHEST-address lane -- st.h 0xAABB to GENCTL would store VECBASE&#x27;s byte. Mandatory mutant + readback row. *** THE SEVEN ODD ARMS ARE OPERATOR-REACHABLE: debugger_cmds.c warns on a misaligned put and then STORES, through memory_rw to the handler. Fix all identically; contract states 5 guest-reachable / 7 operator-reachable. *** IPL is at 0x3e (EVEN) -- its #119 arm is guest-reachable and prints ignored about a read the memcpy already served; fold IPL/MASK in (12 bits). Corrected its OWN 2026-09-02 ruling in three places. Unnamed option member: COMPOSE (per-lane dispatch), with the hazard that it must live INSIDE the arms. C040 kill (legal byte write 0x04 to GENCTL -&gt; exit) has no ledger row. Ten arms / twelve labels. ALL SIX CHECKABLE CLAIMS VERIFIED BY THE MAIN LOOP. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_093835</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-03 — UNKNOWN — *** SEAT DOWN: API 529 Overloaded on claude-opus-5, twice (first firing + the one permitted re-fire). Design pass -- a READING lost, not a measurement; the other seats carry it. NOT agreement. *** — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_093835</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-03 — CONFIRMED — Ten blocks covering twelve labels. Precedent argument AGAINST fixing the odd arms: OB sgirekills says an unreachable terminating site must not be fixed without an executable row -- BUT that case was a dead else-arm no input can reach, a different species from arms the debugger reaches; the operator-reach measurement decides it. Do NOT copy #497&#x27;s 1&lt;&lt;N enum mechanically (the fork records it as collision-prone); use auto-increment + NBITS. Full decline-side row set: pre/post byte snapshots, one message per fresh instance, same-site-twice, five sites once each, TWO INSTANCES -&gt; two messages to distinguish per-instance from static. Two separate findings: the counter arm accepts 8-byte writes that raw-copy through PSCALE and both timer-control bytes; valid aligned wide starts at 0x14/0x18/0x2c hit the default kill (-&gt; pcc2defaultkill). — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_093835</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-03 — UNKNOWN — [NOT-FIRED] *** RESERVED FOR MEASUREMENT by owner ruling; spent on the concurrent pass-14 panel as its builder instead. NOT a seat failure and NOT agreement. *** — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_093835</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-03 — UNKNOWN — *** SEAT DOWN, TOOL FAILURE, TWICE: first firing died after 165 bytes with the CLI&#x27;s own &#x27;Internal error:&#x27;; the one permitted re-fire ran 3 turns / 590 s and exited rc=1 with 478 bytes of narration and no verdict. It confirmed &#x27;ten exit(1) width-kill blocks&#x27; in passing. No quota text, so not a wall; a grok.exe process was alive throughout, so not a stall -- a CLI failure class. NOT agreement. The pcc2 pass-1 roster is therefore 6 of 9 answering (grok x2 tool failure, opus x2 API 529, agy reserved). *** — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_093835</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-03 — CONFIRMED — Fix all arms: uniformity makes a STATIC gate row expressible (grep -c exit(1) -&gt; only default remains), and the reachability proof is an inference future CPU work could silently invalidate. Value rows for reads (composed value, right lane); decline-no-store + latch-once + neighbour-preservation for writes. Found: the C040 byte-write kill survives this fix and must be cited or ten-removed reads as file-clean; pcctwo_interrupt_common&#x27;s default exit is not guest-reachable today; three latch idioms will coexist post-fix and the contract must say why. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_093835</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-03 — MANUAL — Packet-fed. *** P5 WRONG IN BOTH CLAUSES, VERIFIED BY THE MAIN LOOP: the byte arms are NOT reg = idata -- VECBASE &amp; 0xf0, TxICR |= (idata &amp; 0x17) + pending clears, SCCERR = 0, SCC* &amp; 0x1f/0xdf -- and reassert_interrupts is in SIX arms, not two. *** And it derived the cleanest justification of the split: the read path uses raw data in address order (width-correct by construction); every write arm uses idata, which means the addressed byte only at len==1. Reads: delete the discard. Writes: cannot be fixed without per-arm semantics. Decline follows. Two more unnamed members: first-byte-only accept; FAULT&#x27;s feasibility not in the packet (what does the caller do with return 0?). The witness cannot protect the fix: no byte-write row, no value rows. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_093835</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-03 — MANUAL — Packet-fed. Ten blocks / twelve registers conflated; premise 4&#x27;s already-correct unproven (lane order, hardware unknown); premise 2&#x27;s alignment check asserted not inlined. Named per-byte dispatch as unnamed. Fix all seven identically: a kill nothing reaches is a latent kill if the alignment premise ever fails. Honest about what the packet could not settle. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_093835</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-03 — MANUAL — *** FIRST FIRING: HTTPError 429 Too Many Requests -- TWO PANELS LAUNCHED 3 s APART HIT THE SAME CLOUD MODEL. A measured counter-instance to the carrier&#x27;s the-Ollama-spacing-hazard-is-gone: gone for panels minutes apart, NOT for concurrent ones. *** Re-fired once: answered, 7.5 KB. Largely sound; one real defect: premise 4&#x27;s computed-correctly contradicts premise 6&#x27;s no-datasheet -- legality is now settled by the header, lane semantics is not. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260903_093835</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — MANUAL — PASS 13 (Agent, the adjudicator&#x27;s hat).  GO / CLOSE with two L4s: the acc-all arithmetic (same as Opus); the contract&#x27;s &#x27;clock.c not in this tree, NOT independently verified&#x27; is false -- clock.c:172/177/241/242 arm COC on both timers (VERIFIED by the main loop; carried to the pass-14 docstring edit).  Also: the five HUH-arm cites one line off (APPLIED, measured); Astra&#x27;s COVF half under-credited (APPLIED).  Scrutinised its own adopted floor: &#x27;my formulation is right; my APPLICATION wrongly excluded INT&#x27;.  Its &#x27;no partition held on one side only&#x27; checked per ARM, not per CELL -- superseded by opus5/grok/kimi&#x27;s derivation; &#x27;nothing unheld&#x27; is now wrong twice in one round, recorded as a pattern.  Queue order defaultkill-first CONFIRMED both ways by grep (pcc2_genctl is only a struct field in the guest). — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — CONFIRMED — PASS 13 (Agent; chose reading over building because two panels&#x27; seats were on the machine).  Re-derived all eight part-13 scores from the handler and probe source, name for name.  Two in-rule gaps in the pass-13 repair: L2-a the generating set is ONE-SIDED at the two new (label, INT set, own count 0) cells -- `grep ST_B(13&#x27; finds exactly two sessions and each is followed by ONE wide write, 0x0013, so `&amp;&amp; (idata &amp; ICLR)&#x27;, `&amp;&amp; (idata &amp; 0xe0)&#x27;, `&amp;&amp; !(idata &amp; IEN)&#x27; crossed with the cell escape 251/251 by construction (six shapes); L2-b the INT axis was not crossed with the OTHER count -- (T2, p2=0, INT set, p1&gt;0) and its mirror are reachable pure-state cells `pendboth&#x27; never builds (it has no byte write).  L4: F2 item 6&#x27;s correction was itself arithmetically false -- 0x10 &amp; ~0xf0 == 0, acc all trips TxCTL&#x27;s &amp; ~7 and PSCALEADJ&#x27;s print only (APPLIED).  Item 15&#x27;s stated rejection reason (&#x27;t is a judgment input&#x27;) false -- t is the body&#x27;s longest conjunction; the real grounds are cost (seven binary axes at TxICR -&gt; tens of pty cells per arm) and occurs-vs-observed (APPLIED to CHANGELOG + carrier).  Item 1&#x27;s corrected grading RIGHT, confirmed by a second route (the 242-row figures re-derived: 241/242 and 236/242).  Enumeration verified against all twelve bodies: matches.  The docstring straddle VERIFIED by diff (one hunk, docstring).  Prescribed the pass-14 diff: 0x0000/0x0020/0x0018 (ICLR last) at each new cell; the other-count mirror in pendboth (T2 first) + one new T1-first session; the closed product written into the contract.  Census lesson: sibling parity over rows that WRITE at the arm, not rows NAMED for it. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — CONFIRMED — PASS 13 (GPT-6 Astra, max; pointer-fed, 448 KB stream).  Zero newly identified runtime defects in the twelve blocks and the helper; coverage finding: an incomplete adopted floor -- the two missing stable TxICR cells, generating-set obligations completed consistently (incl. the TxCTL 0xfc fixture cell -- DISCLOSED as debt: the count classes are not body-tested partitions under the adopted floor), the record corrected: stale &#x27;the first of four wide writes&#x27; texts (pend2/pend1 nine wide writes, pendboth eight -- carried to pass 14), &#x27;not constructible by a probe&#x27; overstates (any of the seven reasserting arms sets INT, not only DEVICE_TICK -- carried), the working diff is comment + typedef not comment-only (the brief&#x27;s text; the CHANGELOG had it right), appended execution can change `alive&#x27; which the rb4 rows consult (true; disclosed).  Valid measured zero: 0 surviving of 7 mutants on 251 rows -- &#x27;does not establish complete floor coverage&#x27;. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — UNKNOWN — Reserved for measurement (owner ruling 2026-08-30); not a seat failure. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — MANUAL — PASS 13 (grok-4.6 xhigh, --prompt-file; 13.6 KB).  Found the two gaps independently: &#x27;Denominator I did not find closed: generating set at the two new floor cells (IEN-clear / ICLR-set / HUH?-set as wide writes); sticky-INT x other-pending.  A zero that does not list those is zero looked for.&#x27;  Grades them L1 on uncommitted detector material -- ADOPTED as the grading (nothing shipped since b78bb0f).  Also confirmed mut_syntax.py&#x27;s hardcoded anchor as a real check-that-cannot-fail and mut_syntax2.py as the right replacement. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — BELIEVED — [ollama_kimi.txt] TRANSPORT kimi-k3:cloud (SUBSTITUTE, fired as OLLAMA4 beside the CLI on this date -- two transports for one seat; the CLI&#x27;s own entry is separate).  PASS 13 (packet-fed substitute; the CLI answered too -- two transports for one seat on this date, recorded by transport; OLLAMA4 blanked after this panel).  6.7 KB.  Close; caught that &#x27;0x0001 is HUH?-clear at these arms&#x27; is false at VECBASE (0x0001 &amp; ~0xf0 = 0x01) -- L4 applied to the CHANGELOG and carrier. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — BELIEVED — PASS 13 (glm-5.3:cloud, packet-fed).  TWO THINKING BURNS on the 17 KB three-question packet (response empty, done_reason stop, 118-124 KB thinking; kept as ollama_glm.burn.txt / .burn2.txt) -- the fifth seat-failure class, cure as documented: a 2 KB ONE-question packet (brief_pcc2_p13.glm_mini.md) answered on the third firing: (a) INSIDE the floor -- pass 14 is owed (clause 2 is a per-cell requirement); (b) not settleable from the packet.  Recorded as answered on a NARROWER brief than the roster&#x27;s. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — BELIEVED — PASS 13 (deepseek-v4-pro:cloud, packet-fed, 2.8 KB).  Objected that the M_ZINT guard `!((reg &amp; INT) &amp;&amp; p == 0 &amp;&amp; label)&#x27; &#x27;is false in that state so it cannot land the write&#x27; -- REJECTED: the guard being false is exactly the case where the decline is skipped and the write LANDS (measured 0x33).  Right that F2 item 1 named two of seven red rows -- L4 applied. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-09-05 — BELIEVED — PASS 13 (minimax-m3:cloud, packet-fed, 7.4 KB).  Chain can close from the packet; one wording defect in premise 3.  Superseded on closure by the file-reading seats&#x27; derivation. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021741</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">lcabadval</span><span class="ttl">dev_lca.c: SIX chipset registers in DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_ioc) kill the host on a value outside a small accepted set (CONF, TB_ENA, W_BASE0/1, W_MASK0/1) -- plus a seventh exit in the default arm, which this round does NOT close</span><span class="tip">dev_lca.c: SIX chipset registers in DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_ioc) kill the host on a value outside a small accepted set (CONF, TB_ENA, W_BASE0/1, W_MASK0/1) -- plus a seventh exit in the default arm, which this round does NOT close — witness: harness:ENUMERATED from the shipped source, 2026-08-31.  Eleven live terminating calls.  The value guards, each ending in exit(1): `idata &amp; ~1` (:206), `idata &amp; ~IOC_TB_ENA_TEN` (:226), `idata != 0ULL &amp;&amp; idata != 0x300800000ULL` (:241), `idata != 0x700000ULL` (:256), `idata != 0x240000000ULL` (:280), `idata != 0x3ff00000ULL` (:295).  Each diagnostic says so in its own words -- *&quot;(0x%&quot; PRIx64&quot;) from the only implemented value&quot;*.  Plus two range guards that also kill: `dev &gt;= 21` (:129) and `ofs &gt; len` (:163).  NO rung-3 witness: READ, not booted. — note: *** RECORDS CORRECTION 2026-09-06, from RE-DERIVING this row&#x27;s own citations instead of trusting them.  THE
tools\pipeline\matrix.html:6325:*** 8. THE WITNESS IS NOT PENDING -- THE RECIPE EXISTS.  This moves the round off documented-only. ***
tools\pipeline\matrix.html:6627:across the ARM queue**, having just corrected three rows for the Alpha version of it.*</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-06 — GPT-6 Astra, max effort, on a purpose-written assess brief (answer preserved at _scratchpad/codex_lcabadval/ANSWER_astra_20260906.txt; refused the first packet on its content filter and answered the neutralised one).  **IT CORRECTED THE ROW&#x27;S CENSUS AND MY BRIEF&#x27;S, AND I VERIFIED THE SHARPEST CORRECTION BY OPENING THE FILE.**  Comment-aware counting gives **12 textual exits, 11 LIVE**: six value guards, two interrupt, one nonzero-bus, one ISA-range, one IOC-default.  **The `dev &gt;= 21&#x27; guard my brief listed as a live range kill is COMMENTED OUT** -- dev_lca.c has `/*  fatal(...); exit(1);  */` inside it and assigns `dev = 0;` instead.  Verified.  So the brief asked about a dead guard, and the premise-audit opener is what surfaced it.  Also: exactly THREE guards accept a single value (not four), and FOUR diagnostics carry the phrase `from the only implemented&#x27;.  **IT ALSO REFUTED THE CONFOUND AS I STATED IT**, which changes the witness design rather than the defect: `Any interrupt overstates the confound&#x27; -- bus_isa.c (anchor `old_isa_assert == new_isa_assert&#x27;) filters unchanged masked state, so only callbacks that actually PROPAGATE terminate.  The oracle still cannot rest on exit status, but the interference is narrower and testable.  Its witness specification: drive the named IOC cases through the real memory decode with native quadword accesses, and require same-decode liveness, a device-specific signature beyond an ordinary write/read echo, independent value and width recording, state preservation, and latch repetition plus instance controls -- with the oracle validated against separate interrupt-diagnostic fixtures.  It found NO Alpha or LCA regression probe anywhere in the tree, which is why this file has no coverage at all.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — *** THE ROUND&#x27;S BEST ANSWER.  Refuted the row&#x27;s own title without needing the one fact it could not settle, and caught my brief contradicting itself between Q2 and Q3 -- do these fields feed decode or does the emulator not model them?  Both were asserted. ***  The source settles it against me: base/mask/tlb_enable are written and read back and nothing else; only `ioc_conf` is consumed (`bus = d-&gt;ioc_conf &amp; 1`).  **That splits the fix design** -- three arms are pure storage where a decline may keep the store, and the fourth is not.  Also the sharpest design point of the panel: for `W_BASE0` the accepted `0` is the MAXIMALLY ORDINARY write, so an accept row pinned to the exotic magic constant misfires on the most legal write rather than an unusual one.  Named `IOC_TB_ENA_TEN` as the single fact that would close the census, which is exactly the right move for a packet-fed seat. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_053346</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — Derived the accept sets independently and reached the same correction.  Held the line on reachability: named an LCA IOC register specification or PROM source as the one thing that would settle whether these are hardware-legal values or merely the ones this emulator was developed against.  There is no such document in `_scratchpad/`. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_053346</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — Went arm by arm and attached a single named settling fact to each rather than answering around the gaps -- the discipline this project asks of a packet-fed seat. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_053346</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — UNKNOWN — [HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]  The rung-3 seat says a witness IS constructible and specified a full sequence, and it refuted three of this row&#x27;s own records (six value-guarded arms not four; eleven live exit(1) not twelve; three arms of six accept exactly one value, not one of four -- so the ORIGINAL title was closer to right than the correction that overturned it).  It also named a CONFOUND that would make the probe lie: lca_interrupt_assert and lca_interrupt_deassert are bare fatal()+exit(1) with the whole ISA PIC chain wired to them, so ANY interrupt ends the host with the SAME status as the value guards under test.  THE QUESTION FOR THE FLAGSHIP SEAT: given that every row must therefore match the fatal() TEXT rather than the exit status, and given that lcaconfwidth (filed today) means the IOC_CONF arm&#x27;s text can PRINT THE WRONG VALUE, is the text-matching oracle sound at THAT arm -- or must lcaconfwidth&#x27;s printf fix land FIRST, making it a prerequisite of this row rather than a sibling?  Second: the de-escalation clause owes an accept row PER PREDICATE, and the ledger&#x27;s earlier census dropped W_BASE1 and W_MASK1 -- confirm the accept-row set is six, not four.  QUESTION (added 2026-09-08, after codex settled the disposition and left the hardware claim open): The DISPOSITION is now settled by codex against #447&#x27;s actual implementation: decline the out-of-set write and PRESERVE the previous value (the queue&#x27;s option B), with the store moved BELOW the guard -- because today the store runs FIRST (dev_lca.c:233 vs the guard at :236), so merely deleting the exit(1) leaves the bad value STORED and guest-readable.  What is NOT settled, and is this row&#x27;s research question: **what does the real 21066 LCA do with an out-of-set value in these six registers?**  We have NO LCA datasheet on this machine -- `_scratchpad/*.pdf` holds none -- and the only primary source is the OpenBSD 2.2 driver (`_guest-src-openbsd22/sys/arch/alpha/pci/lca_pci.c`), which shows what a GUEST writes and not what the CHIP accepts.  So: (a) is decline-and-preserve defensible as MODELLING, or is it merely the safest thing to do in ignorance -- and should the round SAY the latter rather than imply the former?  (b) The guard&#x27;s accepted sets are themselves unverified: W_MASK0/W_BASE1/W_MASK1 REJECT their own reset value of 0, and the header names 0 as IOC_W_MASK_1M, which suggests 0 is a legal encoding the whitelist omits.  **Is the correct round actually to widen or delete the whitelists rather than to change what happens when they fail?** — evidence: [HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — MANUAL — RUNG-3 ATTEMPT: MADE 2026-08-31 per the owner ruling, by a reading seat.  *** RESULT: A WITNESS IS CONSTRUCTIBLE AND A FULL SEQUENCE IS SPECIFIED -- so this row is NOT documented-only, and `none&#x27; would have meant `did not think to ask&#x27;. ***  Target `-E alpha -e alphabook1 0x4000:/dev/null&#x27;; machine_alpha.c&#x27;s ST_ALPHABOOK1 is the ONLY subtype calling device_add(machine,&quot;lca&quot;).  Construction and debugger-prompt arrival are ALREADY MEASURED elsewhere in this repo -- CHANGELOG #279&#x27;s blast-radius gate lists alphabook1 among the twelve machines reaching the prompt, and gate_asan_sweep.sh&#x27;s AB_EXEMPT lists alpha/3000/300 and NOT alphabook1.  Guest VA is K0SEG (paddr | 0xfffffc0000000000, memory_alpha.c), with the ptbr==0 identity path as a second route.  A guest `stq a1,0(a0)&#x27; = 0xB6300000 reaches DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_ioc) via LS_GENERIC_N -&gt; memory_rw.
