e="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — UNKNOWN — [HELD AWAITING SEAT: codex, grok, kimi, opus5, fable5]  *** THIS MARKER REPLACES FIVE `NOT-FIRED&#x27; SEAT ENTRIES I WROTE EARLIER TODAY, AND REMOVING THEM IS A CORRECTION, NOT TIDYING. ***  `check_stage_panels.py` adds a seat id to the stage&#x27;s set REGARDLESS OF OUTCOME -- only HELD-token and annotated entries are skipped -- so five entries recording that a seat was NOT fired made this stage read **9/9, a complete panel, when three seats had answered**.  The gate went GREEN on a roster I had falsified, which is the seat-failure-counted-as-agreement shape arriving through the bookkeeping rather than through a silent blank.  *The checker&#x27;s own comment predicts it: &quot;otherwise marking a gap would close it.&quot;*  **WHY THESE FIVE ARE HELD, so the marker carries its question rather than a disposition note:**  they are the FILE-READING and Agent seats, deliberately not fired while a measuring seat with time-based oracles was running -- a deferral, not a failure.  **The question they are held for:** grep the fork for an existing precedent before choosing among the six de-fatalisation members for `draw_primitive()`&#x27;s `default:` arm, and say whether FAULT has any in-tree warrant here; then give the smallest edit that breaks a latch+decline fix while still passing a detector built for it.  *Two of the three premises the packet-fed seats refused have since been settled by reading and are recorded on this row: there is NO common tail after the switch, and `op` reads the memset reset value 0 = DE_PRIM_POINT.  The third -- the complete blast radius -- is settled to one certain row and one conditional on wording.*  agy is recorded separately as deliberately not fired under the measurement reservation. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_033247</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — UNKNOWN — *** RESERVED FOR MEASUREMENT by owner ruling.  NOT a seat failure and NOT agreement. *** — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_033247</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  *** THE ROUND&#x27;S BEST FINDING AND IT LANDS AGAINST THE AUTHOR: the 2-of-4 reframing is a PARTITION of the 254/256 claim, not a correction, and recording only the sharper half is the locally-true restatement that hides the defect. ***  Also asked the one checkable caveat nobody else did -- are op bits [31:26] live? -- which on checking WIDENED the defect: the primitive field is bits [25:24] and the mask is [31:24], so a legal LINE or RECTANGLE with a stray high bit also dies.  Named four premises as not settleable from the packet, each with the single fact that would settle it, and separated the all-zeroes CONSTANT from the register&#x27;s RESET VALUE. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_033247</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  Supplied the clause-(d) mutant BEFORE the fix exists -- drop the `!` from the guard, so the latch never sets and the announce never fires while the bit name and the absent exit(1) both still read correct -- AND the row that kills it: two distinct unimplemented primitives in one session, expecting exactly one message.  Precision correction: 254/256 counts MASKED TOP-BYTE CLASSES, not full 32-bit op values. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_033247</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2