same empty table.  Logs: regress/artifacts/gdromcondlies/opus_p2_20260830/</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">exitcensus</span><span class="ttl">exit_census.py&#x27;s BY-ENCLOSING-CONSTRUCT split attributed every call in a plain non-static function to the preceding DEVICE_ACCESS -- inflating the bucket used to rank reachability</span><span class="tip">exit_census.py&#x27;s BY-ENCLOSING-CONSTRUCT split attributed every call in a plain non-static function to the preceding DEVICE_ACCESS -- inflating the bucket used to rank reachability — witness: harness:the pre-existing tools/pipeline/exit_census.py reports dev_sgi_re.c = 21 LIVE, which is the correct answer I spent an hour deriving by hand after a grep gave 25</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">sgireunmapped</span><span class="ttl">dev_sgi_re.c&#x27;s unmatched-address else arm ends the host on ANY width in EITHER direction across 2080 bytes of its own registered window -- one guest `lb` at 0xb5001800 -- and NEITHER #497 nor sgirekills-as-scoped touches it</span><span class="tip">dev_sgi_re.c&#x27;s unmatched-address else arm ends the host on ANY width in EITHER direction across 2080 bytes of its own registered window -- one guest `lb` at 0xb5001800 -- and NEITHER #497 nor sgirekills-as-scoped touches it — commits: a643e18 — witness: probe:regress/artifacts/sgireunmapped/opus_witness_20260830/sgi_re_unmapped_probe.py -- RUNG 3, 32/32, on unmodified `-E sgi -e ip32`.  Every access is a genuine guest instruction via `step`; `put w` writes only scratch RAM and never the device, so the `put d` laundering rule is obeyed.  CONTROLS: liveness (RAM round-trip), DEVICE-SIGNATURE (a 4-byte store to MAPPED 0x1700 triggers #497&#x27;s decline, text only this device emits), a NEIGHBOUR-DEVICE control (de_status returns 0x1e000000 = the four CRIME_DE_*_IDLE bits), a NEGATIVE control (mapped 0x16dc survives), and all five hand-assembled encodings checked against the debugger&#x27;s own `unassemble`.  WIDTHS ENUMERATED RATHER THAN ARGUED: len=1, 4 and 8 all kill, in both directions, across both address runs -- which measures the &quot;no width predicate&quot; claim instead of reading it.  Table 1 complete: base 10/14 (test-first RED), fix 14/14, restore `cmp` vs SEC CLEAN, sentinel TABLE_DONE.  TWO INDEPENDENT TABLES, nine variants each, agreeing: `table1_scores.txt` (TABLE_DONE) and `table2_repaired.txt` (RESCORE2_DONE).  base 10/14 · fix 14/14 · mret0 12/14 · mlatch 13/14 · mwonly 11/14 · mshrink/mshrinkb/mtexshrink 13/14 · mnolatch 13/14.  **They differ on exactly ONE variant and for exactly the predicted reason** -- `mnolatch` was 14/14 in run 1 and is 13/14 in run 2, because run 1&#x27;s row could not fail until the gxprobe pc-cache defect was repaired.  *Two runs disagreeing on one variant for a known reason is stronger evidence than two identical runs.* — note: OPEN, and the committed artifact named in `witness` is the REPRODUCTION -- **no fix has shipped**.  `regress/artifacts/sgireunmapped/opus_witness_20260830/sgi_re_unmapped_probe.py` is the rung-3 witness that LICENSES a fix: it demonstrates the host dying at 32/32 on the committed build, which is test-first working in the right order.  Committing evidence that a defect exists is not the same as repairing it, and the shipped-work heuristic cannot tell them apart -- the same exemption `sgirekills` carries, for the same reason.  *** AND THE ROUND IS NOT MERELY UNSHIPPED, IT IS BLOCKED ON A NAMED OBLIGATION: three accept rows (`accept tlba/tlbb/tlbc`) are UNDISCHARGED because no shrink mutant was built for the TLB windows, and those windows need a DIFFERENT mutant shape -- they are bounded by the next window&#x27;s constant rather than base+size, so shrinking one moves a boundary two arms share. ***  That is L3 and is owed BEFORE the fix ships, so a closure now would be false in two directions at once.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — *** THE STRONGEST ANSWER OF THE ROUND, AND IT ENLARGED THE OPTION SET FROM FOUR MEMBERS TO SIX -- BOTH NEW MEMBERS FOUND IN THE TREE, NOT REASONED. ***  (5) FAULT: `dev_unreadable.c` is a device whose whole access function is `return 0;`, and `machine_sgi.c` installs it TEN times ON THIS MACHINE so absent hardware raises DBE -- verified.  Rejected on EVIDENCE (no CRIME datasheet in _scratchpad, no evidence real CRIME faults there, and a wrong DBE is worse than a wrong 0 because it diverts control flow), not on principle.  (6) BACKED-ACCEPT: invent storage, the `mte_reg[]`/`de_reg[]` idiom in this same file; available for CLIP_IDS, rejected under the addition licence.  It also named a seventh candidate (ALIAS/mirror) and dismissed it.  **AND IT FOUND THE FILE&#x27;S OWN POLICY: the three sibling handlers -- sgi_de, sgi_mte, sgi_de_status -- ALREADY decline unmatched addresses without exit(1), and pristine upstream&#x27;s sgi_de was exit-free too, so the RE catch-all is UPSTREAM RESIDUE and this fix removes the file&#x27;s one exception to its own policy.**  That is a far stronger warrant than &#x27;it is a host kill&#x27;.  Gave TWO latch bits with a better warrant than #497&#x27;s (the house latch is per-MESSAGE-SITE and this arm has two texts), enumerated TWELVE boundary constants and twelve owed accept rows, and found a LATCH-BIT COLLISION escape (1&lt;&lt;5 colliding with LINB_LEN passes all three stated oracles).  ONE CLAIM REFUTED -- see the row note. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_232416</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — (HELD-AWAITING-SEAT/defanged: opus5 -- DISCHARGED 2026-08-31)  The hold was for the rung-3 witness ATTEMPT the lifecycle ruling requires before a round may record itself unwitnessed.  **It did not merely attempt: it BUILT one, 32/32**, with liveness, device-signature, neighbour-device and negative controls, and widths enumerated rather than argued.  It also found THREE escapes, corrected a row of its own that failed for an ADEL rather than a code reason, and diagnosed a defect in the shared probe harness that made one of its rows unable to fail.  *The provisional-adjudication rule was right to hold: the design converged 8/9 and the ninth seat still changed the round -- an accept row at a window BASE cannot see a far-bound move, which no reading seat had noticed.* — evidence: regress/artifacts/sgireunmapped/opus_witness_20260830</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — 1.3 MB.  Independently derived the TEX geometry from the CRIME spec -- 28 entries of 64 bits -- which cross-checks my walk of the shipped code exactly and SHARPENED `sgitexindex` from &#x27;wrong shift&#x27; to &#x27;unit mismatch&#x27;.  Called Q5 a false dichotomy and put the correction best: **&#x27;six real windows&#x27; should read &#x27;six MODELED windows&#x27;** -- CLIP_IDS is a seventh real hardware window with no dispatch.  Listed the six accept-row addresses and the final aligned starts to pin upper-bound drift.  *Its supporting citation is a URL to an external spec, NOT read locally; the local header, struct comment and array arithmetic are what carry it.* — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_232416</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-08-30 — UNKNOWN — *** RESERVED FOR MEASUREMENT by owner ruling.  NOT a seat failure and NOT agreement. ***  The seat check printed it by name; a defect in the SUMMARY line that counted it as a non-answering seat was found and fixed in this same commit. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_232416</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — FILE-READING.  Member 3, splice not return, 2080 confirmed, and reached CLIP_IDS independently: *&#x27;unmapped is not [right]; CRIME_RE_CLIP_IDS at 0x16e0 is a named 32-byte window the cascade never implements.&#x27;*  Said ONE latch bit -- the round&#x27;s only real disagreement, resolved against it by fable5&#x27;s per-message-site warrant. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_232416</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — FILE-READING.  **Independently RE-WALKED all 4096 dispatched addresses against the header constants and confirmed the kill set exactly.**  Also challenged the `(once)` census the brief quoted from the carrier -- it counted 24 where the carrier said 9, AND IT WAS RIGHT; re-derived here by four methods and the carrier is corrected with its deriver inlined. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_232416</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  Correctly flagged that the 2080 enumeration is *&#x27;conditional on window-constant values the packet asserts and never derives&#x27;* -- a fair premise-audit catch: I verified the constants from crmfbreg.h but did not inline that derivation in the brief. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_232416</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  Reached member 3 and TWO direction bits from the packet alone -- the same answer fable5 justified from the tree, by a different route. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_232416</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-30 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  Honestly refused Q5 as unsettleable from the packet and warned that a stale constant there would silently shrink the kill set -- which is exactly what CLIP_IDS turned out to bear on. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260830_232416</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">fbfiqsilent</span><span class="ttl">dev_footbridge.c answers FIQEnable reads with a silent constant 0 while its IRQ twin kills the host -- the whole FIQ column is softer than the IRQ column</span><span class="tip">dev_footbridge.c answers FIQEnable reads with a silent constant 0 while its IRQ twin kills the host -- the whole FIQ column is softer than the IRQ column — witness: harness:READ from the shipped source and the datasheet, 2026-08-30, both sides side by side.  `case FIQ_ENABLE_SET:` is `if (writeflag == MEM_WRITE) d-&gt;fiq_enable |= idata; break;` -- a READ falls through with `odata` untouched, so the tail returns 0.  Its twin `case IRQ_ENABLE_SET:` does `odata = d-&gt;irq_enable;` and then `fatal(); exit(1);`.  Same architectural register (188h/288h, IRQEnable/FIQEnable), opposite failures.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">witnesssilent</span><span class="ttl">13 witnesses are ungated BY DESIGN, so a witness whose arms rot is indistinguishable from one that works -- and n6 is about to rot one</span><span class="tip">13 witnesses are ungated BY DESIGN, so a witness whose arms rot is indistinguishable from one that works -- and n6 is about to rot one — witness: none -- a proposal about test apparatus.  Its motivating instance is measured: fbpending_witness.py scores a row on a death at the site n6 removes, and NO GATE RUNS IT, so nothing will report the breakage.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">agyreservation</span><span class="ttl">the owner&#x27;s agy-reserved-for-measurement ruling lives in the carrier as PROSE and panel.sh knows nothing about it -- so agy was fired in the very next panel</span><span class="tip">the owner&#x27;s agy-reserved-for-measurement ruling lives in the carrier as PROSE and panel.sh knows nothing about it -- so agy was fired in the very next panel — witness: harness:panel_20260830_214609/ -- agy.txt exists in a routine panel fired AFTER the ruling; `grep -ci &#x27;reserved&#x27; panel.sh` returns 0, and the launch at panel.sh&#x27;s AGY block is unconditional.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">gatedevicesplit</span><span class="ttl">gate_arm.sh has become the tree&#x27;s device-probe gate by accretion, and #497 is the FIRST probe in it on a foreign machine AND CPU family</span><span class="tip">gate_arm.sh has become the tree&#x27;s device-probe gate by accretion, and #497 is the FIRST probe in it on a foreign machine AND CPU family — witness: harness:gate_arm.sh runs footbridge, PIT and now an SGI/MIPS probe.  The first two at least share this gate&#x27;s own -E cats machine; the third does not.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</s