x27;s `other kill` row is a DEATH-ONLY oracle -- a one-character change to the text it claims to pin scores 35/35, MEASURED</span><span class="tip">sgi_re_width_probe.py&#x27;s `other kill` row is a DEATH-ONLY oracle -- a one-character change to the text it claims to pin scores 35/35, MEASURED — witness: harness:MEASURED by the #497 pass-2 seat in its own clone, with the prediction filed BEFORE building.  base 35/35 CONTROL=OK; x_othertext (catch-all message text altered, exit(1) untouched) 35/35 with ZERO red rows; x_readtext (one read arm&#x27;s text altered) 34/35, reddening `tlb_a ld kill got=exit1-txt want=exit1+txt`.  The matched pair is the point: it proves the six siblings ARE failable and this one is not.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">holdphase</span><span class="ttl">the hold-marker discriminator was implemented with `&gt;=` where the carrier says LATER, and six holds were cleared by SAME-DATE siblings written by the batch that created the marker</span><span class="tip">the hold-marker discriminator was implemented with `&gt;=` where the carrier says LATER, and six holds were cleared by SAME-DATE siblings written by the batch that created the marker — witness: harness:MEASURED by the codex and opus5 seats on the #497b pass-2 panel, independently, and confirmed here row by row before reverting.  SIX markers were wrongly cleared, ALL of them phase=regress / seat=fable5: ns16550, carrier, es438, sh4sci, wdcdataoutdrain, and wdccdbmidxfer entry [26].  *** THIS FIELD PREVIOUSLY NAMED THE SIXTH AS &#x27;research/opus5, answered at review&#x27;.  THAT IS THE MARKER THE COMMIT **KEPT** -- disposition (b) -- NOT the one it cleared.  Caught by the fable5 seat; I had copied the framing from another seat&#x27;s table without checking which entry it pointed at. ***  widthkillclass was the one CORRECT clearance: held at review, all seven named seats answered at review.  A strictly-later + same-stage test keeps all six and clears that one.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">gxprobepccache</span><span class="ttl">gxprobe cached the pc across `step`, so a driver that stepped without _exec_at() had its next pc assignment silently skipped -- a detector row that could not fail</span><span class="tip">gxprobe cached the pc across `step`, so a driver that stepped without _exec_at() had its next pc assignment silently skipped -- a detector row that could not fail — witness: harness:MEASURED by the #497-family measuring seat and re-verified here.  `gxprobe.py` skips a redundant register assignment when `cache_regs` is on; `_exec_at()` pops the cached pc after stepping, but a driver calling `send(&quot;step&quot;)` DIRECTLY did not -- so its next `set_reg(&quot;pc&quot;, a)` was dropped as redundant.  The transcript is unambiguous: the first access carries a `pc=` line, the second and third do not, and they execute `nop`.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">sgideprimop</span><span class="ttl">dev_sgi_re.c draw_primitive(): a guest-written drawing op ends the host -- 254 of 256 top-byte values reach `default: fatal(); exit(1);`</span><span class="tip">dev_sgi_re.c draw_primitive(): a guest-written drawing op ends the host -- 254 of 256 top-byte values reach `default: fatal(); exit(1);` — witness: probe:regress/artifacts/sgidewidth/opus_witness_20260831 -- MEASURED by the sgidewidth measuring seat as a 24/24 ATTRIBUTION probe on unmodified `-E sgi -e ip32`: identical instruction, identical alignment, offsets differing ONLY in bit 0x800.  At `+0x7xx` (startFlag clear) `sd`/`sw`/`lw`/`ldl`/`ldr` all leave the host ALIVE; at `+0xfxx` (startFlag set) every one gives `exit 1` with `sgi_de: UNIMPLEMENTED drawing op = 0x00000000` and ZERO width messages.  The controlled single-bit difference is what makes it attribution rather than coincidence.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — UNKNOWN — [HELD AWAITING SEAT: codex, grok, kimi, opus5, fable5]  *** THIS MARKER REPLACES FIVE `NOT-FIRED&#x27; SEAT ENTRIES I WROTE EARLIER TODAY, AND REMOVING THEM IS A CORRECTION, NOT TIDYING. ***  `check_stage_panels.py` adds a seat id to the stage&#x27;s set REGARDLESS OF OUTCOME -- only HELD-token and annotated entries are skipped -- so five entries recording that a seat was NOT fired made this stage read **9/9, a complete panel, when three seats had answered**.  The gate went GREEN on a roster I had falsified, which is the seat-failure-counted-as-agreement shape arriving through the bookkeeping rather than through a silent blank.  *The checker&#x27;s own comment predicts it: &quot;otherwise marking a gap would close it.&quot;*  **WHY THESE FIVE ARE HELD, so the marker carries its question rather than a disposition note:**  they are the FILE-READING and Agent seats, deliberately not fired while a measuring seat with time-based oracles was running -- a deferral, not a failure.  **The question they are held for:** grep the fork for an existing precedent before choosing among the six de-fatalisation members for `draw_primitive()`&#x27;s `default:` arm, and say whether FAULT has any in-tree warrant here; then give the smallest edit that breaks a latch+decline fix while still passing a detector built for it.  *Two of the three premises the packet-fed seats refused have since been settled by reading and are recorded on this row: there is NO common tail after the switch, and `op` reads the memset reset value 0 = DE_PRIM_POINT.  The third -- the complete blast radius -- is settled to one certain row and one conditional on wording.*  agy is recorded separately as deliberately not fired under the measurement reservation. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_033247</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">N/A</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — UNKNOWN — *** RESERVED FOR MEASUREMENT by owner ruling.  NOT a seat failure and NOT agreement. *** — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_033247</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  *** THE ROUND&#x27;S BEST FINDING AND IT LANDS AGAINST THE AUTHOR: the 2-of-4 reframing is a PARTITION of the 254/256 claim, not a correction, and recording only the sharper half is the locally-true restatement that hides the defect. ***  Also asked the one checkable caveat nobody else did -- are op bits [31:26] live? -- which on checking WIDENED the defect: the primitive field is bits [25:24] and the mask is [31:24], so a legal LINE or RECTANGLE with a stray high bit also dies.  Named four premises as not settleable from the packet, each with the single fact that would settle it, and separated the all-zeroes CONSTANT from the register&#x27;s RESET VALUE. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_033247</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  Supplied the clause-(d) mutant BEFORE the fix exists -- drop the `!` from the guard, so the latch never sets and the announce never fires while the bit name and the absent exit(1) both still read correct -- AND the row that kills it: two distinct unimplemented primitives in one session, expecting exactly one message.  Precision correction: 254/256 counts MASKED TOP-BYTE CLASSES, not full 32-bit op values. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_033247</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">OK</span><span class="tip">2026-08-31 — CONFIRMED — PACKET-FED.  Refused the no-common-tail premise and answered CONDITIONALLY ON BOTH BRANCHES, naming #498&#x27;s `goto`-to-reach-the-tail as the governing precedent if a tail exists.  Marked the uninitialised-register inference as REASONED rather than READ -- the distinction the author had blurred. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260831_033247</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">pcc2widthkills</span><span class="ttl">dev_pcc2.c has TWELVE width kills -- twice #497&#x27;s six -- every one `if (len != 1) { fatal(); exit(1); }`, so an ordinary word read of a byte register ends the host</span><span class="tip">dev_pcc2.c has TWELVE width kills -- twice #497&#x27;s six -- every one `if (len != 1) { fatal(); exit(1); }`, so an ordinary word read of a byte register ends the host — witness: harness:ENUMERATED from the shipped source, 2026-08-31.  Twelve `if (len != N)` guards in `dev_pcc2.c`, at lines 359, 371, 394, 407, 429, 467, 477, 492, 507, 528, 543 and 563 -- **all twelve are `len != 1` and all twelve end in exit(1)**, checked by walking each guard&#x27;s following block rather than by grepping adjacency.  17 terminating calls in the file overall.  NO rung-3 witness: this is READ, not booted, and there is no mvme88k rig here.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</spa