16 rows but says \"fifteen rows\" and claims 8/23 (8 green = 15 red). The actual table: 7/23 with 16 red listed. So the prediction was off by one: predicted 15 red/8 green, measured 16 red/7 green. The brief says \"A miss in the SAFE direction is recorded\" \u2014 predicting fewer red than measured (predicted red stays green = unsafe; predicted green that goes red = safe miss). Here prediction said 15 red; measurement had 16 red. The extra red row is... let me count the difference.\n\nPrediction red list for M_EXIT: named wr, named wr msg (n/a), named rd, named rd msg, named rd srvd, inword wr, unnamed wr, ieicr rdawr, ieerr rdawr, latch sameoff, latch twooff, latch rw one, alias 0x6a, alias msg, dir wr text, dir rd text. That's 16 items listed but annotated \"(host exits on the first uncased access in each session: fifteen rows)\". Hmm \u2014 maybe one of the listed items is not a red? E.g., \"named wr msg (n/a)\"? Both \"named wr msg (n/a)\" and... hmm. Let me count: 1 named wr, 2 named wr msg, 3 named rd, 4 named rd msg, 5 named rd srvd, 6 inword wr, 7 unnamed wr, 8 ieicr rdawr, 9 ieerr rdawr, 10 latch sameoff, 11 latch twooff, 12 latch rw one, 13 alias 0x6a, 14 alias msg, 15 dir wr text, 16 dir rd text. Sixteen items, but the parenthetical says \"fifteen rows\" and the header says 8/23 (=15 red). So the prediction internally lists 16 but claims 15 \u2014 maybe one is expected n/a not red? Which one? \"named wr msg (n/a)\" \u2014 if the host exits BEFORE the arm's message... no wait, M_EXIT restores exit(1) \u2014 presumably after printing the old debug line? If M_EXIT restores the ORIGINAL code (debug + exit(1)), then \"named wr msg\" would be 1 (the debug line prints before exit) \u2014 wait, but pre-fix witness showed \"ieicr st.b msg 1\" \u2014 the message printed. So under M_EXIT, msg rows would be 1 (red? the expected value under the fix is 1 too!). Hmm wait \u2014 the expected msg count under the fix is 1 (one latched announce). Under M_EXIT (original code