regress\artifacts\pcc2defaultkill\pass2_seats\codex.txt:2549:GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json:28274:   "state_note": "Filed on pass 2; addendum 2026-09-04 (Opus, pass 8): SCCTXIACK 0x25 has no case at all and SCCRXIACK's body runs on reads.  The same ACCEPT shape pcc2widthkills turned on, at a different predicate.  Filed in OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md (dated tail, `### pcc2defaultkill`, line 14290 as of 2026-09-04); this row added 2026-09-04 so the dashboard shows it -- the bug file had it, the ledger did not.  PROMOTED med -> HIGH 2026-09-04 by the fix-review adjudication (Fable 5.1, ranked FIRST; GPT-6 Astra concurs HIGH): the unimplemented offsets are real PCC2 registers the in-tree guest driver writes -- if_ie.c:609 `pcc2_lancirq = ...' (0x2a), :612 `pcc2_lancerrirq' (0x2b), :655 `pcc2_lancerrstat' (0x28), verified by grep in _guest-src-openbsd22 -- and any access to them reaches default: exit(1).  This note first said the cheapest witness was `put b 0xfff4202a, 0' -> host exit: MEASURED FALSE 2026-09-05 (put b never reaches a DM_DEFAULT arm; it survives and prints nothing) -- the witness is a GUEST st.b/ld.bu.  Option set to bring to pass 1: DECLINE + latched announce vs BACKED ACCEPT (the register array already backs every offset and the memcpy read path already serves it) vs FAULT; the READ side dies today too.  RE-BASED 2026-09-05: the Fable design seat found (main loop verified: machine_mvme88k.c:106 `unreadable' at 0xfff46000; if_ie.c:407-409 badpaddr match) that if_ie never attaches on this model, so the driver's PCC2 writes never run; HIGH/FIRST rests on the measured rung-3 witness (guest st.b/ld.bu to IEICR -> exit 1; put b does not reach the arm; 7/13 on the committed build, `regress/artifacts/pcc2defaultkill/witness_20260905/`) and severity.  Pass-1 panel dir _scratchpad/panel_20260905_021751.  PASS-1 PANEL CONVERGED (2026-09-05, panel_20260905_021751 + Opus/Fable): READ side keep the served byte with a latched 'served 0x%02x' announce (it is a default, not a computed value: not member 4); WRITE side MEMBER 3, DECLINE + per-offset latched fatal() (once), NOT backed accept (the file's own cased siblings -- SCCERR write-to-clear, the ICRs mask+reassert, the read-only PSCALECNT/SPEED/IACKs -- contradict a blanket store; the addition licence is unmet; it would add a bounded write into pcctwo_reg[] reachable at 0x3d).  The Opus seat BUILT both and measured the 13-row witness 13/13 under BOTH -- disposition-blind -- so the detector owes a read-after-write row in ONE session (measured A 0x0 vs B 0x5a, cased-sibling control 0x0/0x0).  if_ie never attaches (unreadable at 0xfff46000; ie_setupram early return at if_ie.c:561-564); ie0 IS configured in conf/M187 and conf/NFS (the brief's conf grep was wrong).  Unresolved: whether the real PCC2 folds 0x40..0xfff (no MVME manual on disk; fork PCC2_SIZE 0x40 vs guest header 0x1000).  Cross-round: fix pcc2c040kill BEFORE any round implements a PCC2 IACK arm (the SCCRXIACK arm runs on READS and the console driver reads it -- routine entry into the C040 path).  PASS-1 PANEL COMPLETE 9/9 (2026-09-05 02:17-03:27; codex via a re-worded copy after a provider refusal; three cloud seats via one re-fire after a concurrent-panel 429).  CONVERGED: fix A (Opus, measured) -- reads keep the served byte with a latched 'served 0x%02x' announce, writes DECLINED with a per-offset latched fatal() (once); no backed accept; IACKs declined; the in-word bytes disclosed as a width matter.  NEW: the alias is DOCUMENTED (Motorola VMESBCP2 Table 6-1, codex); IEERR SCLR reads as zero (a store would fabricate status).  Implementation drafted (fix_pcc2_default.py + a 23-row detector reusing the width probe's session()); ships after the width chain's pass-13 commit.",
