web search: Alpha OSF PALcode swpctx v0 a0 registers preserved clobbered
codex
Two premises need correction: the identifier change leaves a0 holding the incoming context address, not the old context; and three of the eight textual v0 assignments are inside `#if 0`. The full wrapper does return v0. The architecture manual also leaves a0’s post-call value unspecified, so no extra clobber is required. I’m checking whether Alpha startup permits guest execution.
