regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:246:#  makes the identity map die on the FIXED build rather than on the defective one.  **No nonzero
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:247:#  value anywhere in that field survives either polarity**, so K0SEG is not the better option -- it
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:248:#  is the only one.
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:249:#
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:250:#  K0SEG is checked BEFORE `base' is read, so a K0SEG access is immune to whatever `apcb_ptbr'
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:251:#  holds.  Code, both PCBs and the pointer vector therefore all live there.
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:252:#
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:253:#  *** THE BOOTSTRAP, because lda/ldah build 32-bit constants and K0SEG needs bit 63..42: ***
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:254:#  the 64-bit pointers are written into memory with the debugger's `put d' (64-bit; note `put q' is
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:255:#  128-bit in this debugger) and the guest loads them with ONE identity-mapped `ldq' issued while
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:256:#  `ptbr' is still zero.  After that every address the guest uses is a K0SEG value held in a
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:257:#  register, and nothing depends on translation state again.
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:261:#  *** EVERY ADDRESS HERE WAS OUTSIDE RAM UNTIL A CODE REVIEW SAID SO, AND THE FAILURE WOULD
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:262:#  HAVE BEEN SILENT AND GREEN. ***  The machine is built with `-M 64' = 64 MB, and these were
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:263:#  at 0x200xxxxx (512 MB+).  K0SEG translation is `vaddr & 0x3ffffffffff', so the K0SEG idea
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:264:#  survives contact with alpha_translate_v2p -- but the PHYSICAL BACKING does not.
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:265:#
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:266:#  `memory_warn_about_unimplemented_addr' only halts when `halt_on_nonexistant_memaccess' is
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:267:#  set, i.e. under `-T'.  WITHOUT IT: writes succeed and are DISCARDED, and reads RETURN
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:268:#  ZEROS.  An instruction fetch of zeros is a real instruction -- `call_pal 0'.
regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:269:#
